35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, I can't believe it! We are spending a fortune on just moving things and making custom mounts. It's a total money pit!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"My findings are even more worrying. The lab is practically empty, and our volunteers are already stretched thin with other commitments.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shion,,"It seems we've been chasing prestige. The data shows that static displays are dead. People want movement, activity, and human presence.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The building is struggling. The suspended bay has a strict weight limit, and the evening hires are causing more wear than we can manage.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,It seems we are all seeing the same pattern. The logistics of bringing in distant pieces are far more fragile than we like to admit.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shizue, exactly! If we bring in too many loans, the transport and the custom mounts will eat the whole budget before we even open.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, it's not just the money. If we choose a complex exhibition, who is going to do the conservation work? The backlog is already critical.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Victoria, then we should choose something that doesn't require a lab. Something dynamic that engages the visitor without needing a thousand fragile cases.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shion, ""dynamic"" often means heavy equipment or high foot traffic. We cannot ignore that the floor is already under significant stress.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,I've noticed that the paperwork for international loans is where we often stumble. Perhaps we should look for something more local or manageable?,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,I'm definitely leaning toward something that doesn't need expensive custom mounts or crazy shipping costs. Let's keep it simple and affordable!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,I must insist on a proposal that requires minimal conservation and doesn't rely on a volunteer force that is already working elsewhere.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shion,,"Simplicity is fine, but boredom is a crime. If we don't have something that draws people back, the exhibition is a failure regardless of cost.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Asuka,,We must prioritize a proposal that respects the weight limits of the suspended bay and doesn't interfere with the gallery's basic function.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"I agree. A peaceful, well-organized exhibition is much better than a grand one that arrives late and leaves us all exhausted.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
