60,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Option A looks great! Local items mean low transport costs, and textiles don't need expensive custom mounts. It's a budget dream!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"I am very concerned about Option D. A ""working conservation bench"" is a fantasy when the lab is already drowning in a backlog.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shion,,Option A and D both have human elements. A and D are far more likely to bring people back than the static displays of Option C.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option B is out. Overhead rigging and kinetic works in the suspended bay are a structural risk we cannot afford right now.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Option A is so lovely. Local loans mean no shipping cut-off nightmares and no stressful customs delays. It's a very safe, gentle choice.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Asuka, I agree about B. And @Victoria, D sounds like a nightmare for the staff. A is just so much more sensible for our wallet!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, I agree. Option A relies on craftspeople for demonstrations, which takes the pressure off our exhausted internal staff and volunteers.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Victoria, exactly. The ""demonstration sessions"" in A are the key. It gives the visitors a reason to return, which is what we've been missing.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Asuka,,Option A is the only one that doesn't threaten the floor or the bay. Textiles are lightweight and the layout is flexible.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shizue,,It's a wonderful way to celebrate our community too. No one has to apologize for a missing crate if the artist is just down the road.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,"I'm totally sold on A. It's cheap, it's easy, and it's cheerful! Let's do it!","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I support A. It is the only option that doesn't pretend we have a full staff. It uses external expertise to fill the gap.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shion,,"I'll vote for A. It satisfies my requirement for human activity and movement, and it doesn't seem to annoy any of you.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I agree. It is the most logical choice given the structural constraints and the need to maintain the gallery's general utility.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I am very happy we've found something we all agree on. It will be a very peaceful season for everyone involved.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
